\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Japan Govt: Rapid Yen Rise Or Prolonged Strength Is Problem That Can't Be Overlooked\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2010\par 03:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 9 Sep 2010 21:33 EDT *DJ  Japan Govt: Yen Strength Has Negative Impact On Econ, Fincl Conditions\par \par \uc2 9 Sep 2010 21:33 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Govt: To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  If Necessary\par \par \uc2 9 Sep 2010 21:39 EDT *DJ  Japan Govt Makes \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Statement In Econ Package Announcement\par \par \uc2 9 Sep 2010 21:43 EDT *DJ  Japan Govt: Expect "Appropriate, Flexible" BOJ Policy To Support Econ\par \par \uc2 Corrected September 9, 2010 21:58 ET (0158 GMT)\par \par \uc2 9 Sep 2010 21:43 EDT *DJ  Japan Govt: To Keep Close Contact With BOJ To Stop Deflation\par \par \uc2 9 Sep 2010 21:57 EDT *DJ  CORRECT: Japan Govt: Expect "Appropriate, Flexible" BOJ Policy To Support Econ\par \par \uc2 9 Sep 2010 22:09 EDT DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Government: To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  If Necessary\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Japanese government said Friday it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed to curb a rise in the yen that it warns could disrupt the economy and financial conditions.\par \par \uc2 "A rapid or prolonged strengthening in the yen is a problem that cannot be overlooked, given its negative impact on the stability of the economy and financial conditions," the government said in a statement accompanying an announcement of a Y915 billion stimulus package to support the economy.\par \par \uc2 "The government will take decisive steps, including \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when necessary," the government said.\par \par \uc2 The government also kept the heat on the Bank of Japan to do more to stop consumer price deflation, which has ravaged Japan's economy on and off for years, hindering any sustainable recovery.\par \par \uc2 The government said it will keep in close contact with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the aim of conquering deflation, adding that it expects "appropriate and flexible" monetary policy management to support Japan's economy.\par \par \uc2 -By Juro Osawa, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2794; juro.osawa@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 09, 2010 22:09 ET (02:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100910e69a000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
