\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2010\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA TRADE SURPLUS NARROWS; SURPLUS WITH US STILL HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus narrowed sharply to $20.03 billion in August, but its surplus with the U.S. accounted for 90% of the total, widening from about two thirds in July, government data showed Friday. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =JAPAN UNVEILS Y915B STIMULUS, ANALYSTS CALL IT HALF-HEARTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government Friday announced a Y915 billion stimulus package aimed at helping the export-driven economy deal with domestic deflation, a surging yen and a slowdown in overseas markets. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN LIFTS 2Q GDP AS FIRMS RAMP UP CAPITAL SPENDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government Friday raised its reading for the country's second-quarter economic growth rate to an annualized 1.5% from the initial reading of a 0.4% rise thanks to continued improvement in corporate capital spending. (published 0214 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA'S AUGUST URBAN PROPERTY PRICES UNCHANGED VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property prices in 70 of China's large and medium-sized cities were unchanged in August compared with July, but were up 9.3% from a year earlier, the National Bureau of Statistics said Friday. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ ALREADY WORRIED ABOUT YEN IN EARLY AUG, MINUTES SHOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's policy board members were already becoming increasingly concerned about the rising yen at their regular meeting in August, the meeting minutes released Friday showed. This growing discomfort foreshadowed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to ease policy further at an emergency meeting later in the month. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOVERNMENT: TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government said Friday it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if needed to curb a rise in the yen that it warns could disrupt the economy and financial conditions. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER NODA: EXPECT BOJ TO ACT WHEN NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister put renewed pressure on the Bank of Japan Friday, saying the government hopes central bankers will meet their promise to take proper action when needed to support the nation's economy. (published 0240 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ TRADE DATA HERALD DIMMER OUTLOOK AS EXPORT ENGINE SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's second-quarter terms of trade showed a more-subdued-than-forecast increase in export prices, signalling a slowdown in one of the key engines that has been driving the economy's recovery, according to economists. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN BANK MINISTER: INCUBATOR BANK FAILURE UNLIKELY TO HURT FINANCIAL SYSTEM STABILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Financial Services Minister Shozaburo Jimi said Friday he wasn't very concerned about the impact that the failure of the Incubator Bank of Japan would have on the nation's financial system. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PHILIPPINES SELLS $1B GLOBAL PESO BOND; SEES STRONG DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine government on Thursday raised the equivalent of $1 billion through the sale of its first ever peso-denominated global bond, attracting investors with a yield of 5%, according to bankers close to the transaction. (published 2238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND TO ISSUE 2025 INFLATION-INDEXED BOND AS EARLY AS NOV \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand Debt Management Office said Friday it will launch a September 2025 inflation-indexed bond program as early as November. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BRAZIL WILL TAKE MEASURES TO STOP REAL OVERVALUING - ESTADO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's government will take measures to halt the excessive gains of the real against other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Finance Minister Guido Mantega said Thursday, according to the local Estado newswire. (published 2257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: FIX CONSUMER DEBT RELIEF, FIX THE ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When Joe Bonadio negotiated a 69% reduction in $54,000 of credit card debt this year, his most valuable tool was a caller ID box with ring controller made by JF Technical Developing Co. (published 1956 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS DOWN AS DOLLAR STABILIZES VS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options declined in Tokyo Friday, as demand eased for protection against fluctuations and further falls in the exchange rate with the dollar stabilizing slightly above where it was against the yen in New York late Thursday. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-09-10 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100910e69a000b3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex1