\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2010\par 05:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA AUGUST TRADE SURPLUS $20.03 BLN; MARKET EXPECTED SURPLUS $30.0 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus narrowed to $20.03 billion in August from $28.7 billion in July and was smaller than economists' expectations of a $30.0 billion surplus. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =JAPAN UNVEILS Y915B STIMULUS, ANALYSTS CALL IT HALF-HEARTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government Friday announced a Y915 billion stimulus package aimed at helping the export-driven economy deal with domestic deflation, a surging yen and a slowdown in overseas markets. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN LIFTS 2Q GDP AS FIRMS RAMP UP CAPITAL SPENDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government Friday raised its reading for the country's second-quarter economic growth rate to an annualized 1.5% from the initial reading of a 0.4% rise thanks to continued improvement in corporate capital spending. (published 0214 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA'S AUGUST URBAN PROPERTY PRICES UNCHANGED VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property prices in 70 of China's large and medium-sized cities were unchanged in August compared with July, but were up 9.3% from a year earlier, the National Bureau of Statistics said Friday. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ RELEASES MINUTES FOR AUGUST 9-10 POLICY BOARD MEETING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concern over recent yen rises had already increased among Bank of Japan policy board members at their August meeting before its easing decision later that month, according to minutes of the meeting released Friday by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOVERNMENT: TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government said Friday it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if needed to curb a rise in the yen that it warns could disrupt the economy and financial conditions. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER NODA: EXPECT BOJ TO ACT WHEN NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister put renewed pressure on the Bank of Japan Friday, saying the government hopes central bankers will meet their promise to take proper action when needed to support the nation's economy. (published 0240 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ TRADE DATA HERALD DIMMER OUTLOOK AS EXPORT ENGINE SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's second-quarter terms of trade showed a more-subdued-than-forecast increase in export prices, signalling a slowdown in one of the key engines that has been driving the economy's recovery, according to economists. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN BANK MINISTER: INCUBATOR BANK FAILURE UNLIKELY TO HURT FINANCIAL SYSTEM STABILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Financial Services Minister Shozaburo Jimi said Friday he wasn't very concerned about the impact that the failure of the Incubator Bank of Japan would have on the nation's financial system. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PHILIPPINES SELLS $1B GLOBAL PESO BOND; SEES STRONG DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine government on Thursday raised the equivalent of $1 billion through the sale of its first ever peso-denominated global bond, attracting investors with a yield of 5%, according to bankers close to the transaction. (published 2238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BRAZIL WILL TAKE MEASURES TO STOP REAL OVERVALUING - ESTADO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's government will take measures to halt the excessive gains of the real against other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Finance Minister Guido Mantega said Thursday, according to the local Estado newswire. (published 2257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: FIX CONSUMER DEBT RELIEF, FIX THE ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When Joe Bonadio negotiated a 69% reduction in $54,000 of credit card debt this year, his most valuable tool was a caller ID box with ring controller made by JF Technical Developing Co. (published 1956 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-09-10 0301GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100910e69a0006a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
