\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 9\b0\par\par\uc2 1,910 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: BANK OF KOREA, IN SURPRISE, STANDS PAT; SIGNALS HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea kept interest rates steady Thursday, defying expectations of a rate hike, but signaled it will gradually tighten policy in coming months to keep inflation in check. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 14 OF 15 ANALYSTS SAY BANK OF KOREA COULD UP RATES IN OCT - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea is likely to resume its tightening cycle in October after holding rates steady for two consecutive months to contain inflationary pressures despite higher external risks, analysts said Thursday. (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSSIE JOB MARKET ON FIRE, UPS CHANCE OF NOV. HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's job market keeps growing, adding 30,900 jobs in August, driving the unemployment rate down to 5.1% and putting the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  on notice that it may need to resume hiking interest rates soon. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN NODA: CONDUCTING VARIOUS SIMULATIONS ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ACTION \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister kept the threat of yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alive Thursday, saying the authorities "are conducting various simulations" to curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: MAS TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF US DOLLAR STAYS BELOW S$1.34010-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is poised to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, selling the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the second time, this month if the U.S. dollar trades "consistently" below S$1.3410, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOV: MORE JGB BUYING MAY HAVE ADVERSE EFFECTS ON MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa on Thursday reiterated his reluctance to boost the size of its Japanese government bond buying from the market, saying such a move could drive up long-term yields if investors think the BOJ is trying to finance fiscal spending. (published 0222 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER: PLAN TO CHECK CHINA'S INTENTION BEHIND JGB BUYING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Minister of Finance Yoshihiko Noda said Thursday the government is closely monitoring China's stepped-up buying of Japanese government debt and he will check with Beijing on the reasons behind its move. (published 0140 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN'S BIG COMPANY'S SENTIMENT WORSENS FOR OCT-DEC QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Large Japanese companies have become cautious in their outlook for the economy and business conditions in the October-December quarter, as concerns grow about the strong yen and a slowing global economy, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  survey showed Thursday. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PHILIPPINES JULY EXPORTS SURPRISE WITH 36% GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine July exports surprised on the upside, rising 36% from a year earlier and extending a recovery that started last November on the back of a rebound in electronic shipments--a development that bodes well for sustained robust growth of the domestic economy, at least into the third quarter. (published 0347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: MALAYSIA JULY INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 3.2% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's industrial output expanded 3.2% in July from a year earlier because of increases in manufacturing and electricity output, official data released Thursday show. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RBA'S DEBELLE SAYS DISLOCATION ON DECLINE IN AUSTRALIA MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's financial markets have operated with less dislocation than other parts of the world over the past three years and continue to do so, Guy Debelle, assistant governor at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Thursday. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES TO PRICE 10-YEAR PSEO BOND AS EARLY AS TODAY - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine government may price a benchmark-sized peso-denominated global bond as early as Thursday, a source privy to the bond issuance said. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA HYDRO TO SELL 5-YEAR DOLLAR BENCHMARK-SIZE BOND -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-run Korea Hydro & Nuclear Power Co. plans to sell a benchmark-sized U.S.-dollar bond, two people familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS: FISCAL DISCIPLINE TEST FOR AUSTRALIA'S MINORITY GOVERNMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's minority government will need to operate within tight fiscal guidelines if it's to meet ambitious budgetary surplus plans while at the same time doling out sweeteners to lawmakers on whose support it depends. (published 2355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: CHINA AUGUST CPI LIKELY HIGHEST SINCE OCTOBER 2008 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer price index likely rose at its fastest rate in nearly two years in August as floods and unusually hot weather for the month pushed up food prices, but economists expect the increases in the CPI to moderate in coming months as weather conditions return to normal. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: SINGAPORE'S GIC LOGISTICS UNIT TO RAISE UP TO US$3 BLN IN IPO - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global Logistic Properties Ltd., a real estate unit of sovereign wealth fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., is expected to list on the Singapore Exchange on Oct. 15 in an initial public offering that could raise up to US$3 billion, a person familiar with the transaction said Thursday. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S ACCC MAINTAINS OPPOSITION TO NAB'S BID FOR AXA ASIA PACIFIC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's competition regulator continued its opposition to \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s proposed A$13.3 billion bid for wealth management company rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 AXA Asia Pacific Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Thursday, dealing a heavy blow to the bank's plans to become the country's largest wealth manager. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =3RD UPDATE: TOTAL BUYS 20% OF PROPOSED AUSTRALIA LNG PROJECT FOR A$867M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Santos Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Total S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has bought 20% of its proposed coal seam gas export joint venture for around A$867 million, giving the French oil giant skin in a second Australian project and its first major investment in unconventional gas. (published 0631 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MEDICAL SYSTEMS SEEKS UP TO HK$1.01 BLN IN HK LISTING - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pharmaceutical firm China Medical Systems Holdings Co. is seeking to raise up to HK$1.01 billion in a Hong Kong initial public offering later this month, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Thursday. (published 0040 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ SHORTLISTS 14 FIRMS FOR FIRST STAGE OF BROADBAND ROLLOUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Thursday announced 14 parties were on the shortlist to participate in its NZ$3 billion ultra-fast broadband initiative. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANA: TO LAUNCH NEW LOW-COST CARRIER WITH FIRST EASTERN, OTHERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All Nippon Airways Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it will launch a low-cost carrier with Hong Kong-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 First Eastern Investment Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and others, becoming the first Japanese carrier to operate both budget and conventional services. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: HYUNDAI UNVEILS THE BLUEON, SOUTH KOREA'S 1ST ELECTRIC CAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday unveiled the BlueOn, the first-ever pure electric vehicle for the South Korean market, which the government hopes will include one million electric cars by 2020. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WHARF BUYS SITE IN SHANGHAI FOR CNY4.83 BLN IN LAND AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property-to-ports conglomerate Wharf Ltd. bought a parcel of land in Shanghai for CNY4.83 billion at a land auction, the company said in a statement Wednesday. (published 2353 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 VIRGIN BLUE\f28 \uc2 \f2  WORKING WITH DELTA, US GOVERNMENT TO ADDRESS CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Virgin Blue Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it will work with the U.S. Department of Transportation over the coming two weeks to address the Obama administration's concerns over its planned tie-up with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Delta Air Lines Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on flights between Australia and the U.S. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NISSAN LOOKING AT RAMPING UP THAI PRODUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is considering ramping up production capacity at its plant in Thailand, a market it sees as having potential for significant growth, the head of Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AEVUM CONSIDERS MERGER PLAN WITH FKP PROPERTY UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aevum Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it has held talks with \f28 \uc2 \f2 FKP Property Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  about a possible merger with FKP's listed unit \f28 \uc2 \f2 Forest Place Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . as it looks at alternatives to the A$266.4 million bid from Stockland that it rejected. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: JANUS CAPITAL EYES ASIA GROWTH; ON LOOKOUT FOR NON-US HEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As part of an increased focus on international business, U.S. asset manager \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janus Capital Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is bulking up its Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHANDA INTERACTIVE ENTERTAINMENT 2ND-QUARTER NET DOWN 60% AT $24.8 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shanda Interactive Entertainment Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its second-quarter net profit fell 60% from a year earlier as higher expenses more than offset an increase in revenue. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KT TO START OFFERING UNLIMITED DATA SERVICES FRIDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KT Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it will begin offering unlimited data services Friday to meet the soaring demand for high-speed data caused by the sales boom in smart phones and other digital gadgets. (published 0135 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GUJARAT PIPAVAV SHARES DEBUT AT INR56.25, UP 22% FROM IPO PRICE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gujarat Pipavav Port Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday began trading on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombay Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  at a 22% premium to their initial public offer price. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; CHINA BANKS, PROPERTY COS FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Thursday though Chinese banks and property developers fell on persistent concerns that Beijing would roll out further tightening measures. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SAUDI TO SUPPLY FULL OCT TERM CRUDE TO ASIAN BUYERS -TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-09-10 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabian Oil Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will likely supply full contracted crude volumes to Asian buyers in October, as at least three regional refiners have already been notified by the company that they will receive full allocations, traders said Thursday. (published 0427 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: KUWAIT OCT CRUDE OSP AT OMAN-DUBAI MINUS $2.30/BBL -TRADER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kuwait Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has posted its crude-oil official selling price for October term supply to Asia at $2.30 a barrel below the average of Oman and Dubai assessments, a trader said Thursday. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN OSAKA GAS: TO MAKE METHANE FROM LOW-GRADE COAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Osaka Gas Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it will develop a technology to produce methane, the chief component of natural gas, from low-grade coal to diversify its supply sources from current conventional liquefied natural gas producers. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =RUBBER LEADS CHINA COMMODITY FUTURES DOWN; EXCHANGE DENIES PROBE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Natural rubber futures led China commodity markets on a sharp slide Thursday, even as Shanghai bourse authorities denied market speculation of a crackdown on the rubber futures trade. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA SEP 1-10 PALM OIL EXPORTS UP 1.2% ON MONTH -INTERTEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's palm oil exports in the first 10 days of September rose 1.2% from a month earlier to 396,684 metric tons, according to an estimate by cargo surveyor Intertek Agri Services Thursday. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA JUNE 1-SEPT. 8 MONSOON RAINS 1% ABOVE AVERAGE - WEATHER OFFICE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Widespread showers in the past few days have brought India's monsoon rains to 1% above average from the start of the season on June 1, according to the state-run India Meteorological Department. (published 0343 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANGLADESH TO ISSUE TENDER TO IMPORT 50,000 TONS WHEAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bangladesh plans to issue a tender to import around 50,000 metric tons wheat later Thursday, a government official said. (published 0623 GMT) [ 09-09-10 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100909e699000na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
