\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 :Euro Slightly Down;Irish T-Bill Auction Underpins\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Hastings   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 711 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 12:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The euro is flat to a little lower Thursday after Ireland's latest T-bill auction proved relatively successful.\par \par \uc2 The country raised about EUR400 million in six- and eight-month treasury bills at yields slightly below what the market anticipated, suggesting that international demand for Irish paper remains relatively strong.\par \par \uc2 The yen, meanwhile, was also benefiting from increased speculation that the Japanese won't consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance until after leadership elections are held by the ruling Democratic Party of Japan Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supported over the last day or so by a successful bond auction in Portugal Wednesday and a string of relatively positive economic developments elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 However, much of the support started to ebb away when it became clear that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been actively purchasing euro-zone bonds in an effort to provide support. Some estimates suggested that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought EUR300 million of paper so far this week.\par \par \uc2 Also, the cost of credit default swaps for several peripheral debtors continued to push to new record highs Tuesday. Since then, CDS prices as well as yield spreads have largely stabilized.\par \par \uc2 Underlying global sentiment was still underpinned, however, by a largely positive Beige Book from the U.S. Federal Reserve Wednesday that suggested that the U.S. economy is still expanding even if it is doing so with a slower momentum. The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  also contributed a certain amount of bullish sentiment with its decision to hike interest rates by 25 basis points. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did also acknowledge that Canadian economic growth is likely to be slightly more gradual than the bank had projected back in July.\par \par \uc2 Australian unemployment provided additional cheer about the global economy, with the jobless rate falling to 5.1% in August from 5.3% in July. The market had been looking for a fall to only 5.2%.\par \par \uc2 While the euro bounced around waiting to see how the Irish auction fared, the yen was the other major focus of the market.\par \par \uc2 Although Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda acknowledged that the ministry is looking at various \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "simulations," the market is speculating that nothing will happen until after the DPJ chooses a new leader on Tuesday. The new leader will automatically become prime minister and means that the current prime minister, Naoto Kan, could be replaced by his main contender in the election, Ichiro Ozawa, who has expressed explicit support for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the risks of any imminent move to stop the yen's advance appears unlikely, especially after Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaaki Shirakawa denied that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was discussed in meetings with the government.\par \par \uc2 See how the dollar has slipped against the yen:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4566"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4566}}}\par \par \uc2 This helped to give the yen more upside potential with the dollar falling to Y83.63 by midmorning from Y83.92 late Wednesday in New York, according to EBS.\par \par \uc2 The euro was also down at Y106.36 from Y106.72 but was hardly changed at $1.2717, compared with $1.2716.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to CHF1.0154 from CHF1.0122, while the pound fell to $1.5393 from $1.5465.\par \par \uc2 Sterling was coming under pressure as the market waits for the Bank of England to confirm that its is leaving interest rates unchanged and that quantitative easing will not be increased at this stage.\par \par \uc2 The pound was also hurt by the latest U.K. trade report which showed the country's trade deficit widening to record GBP8.7 billion in July. The market had been looking for it to widen to only GBP7.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Nicholas Hastings, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9493; nick.hastings@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 09-09-10 1002GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100909e69900109\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
