\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Japanese policymakers' remarks on yen, BOJ\b0\par\par\uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 09:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 9 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said on Thursday that monetary authorities are conducting various simulations on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will take decisive steps on the yen's rise when necessary.\par \par \uc2 Following are recent key quotes by Bank of Japan and government officials:\par \par \uc2 FINANCE MINISTER YOSHIHIKO NODA, Sept. 9, in parliament\par \par \uc2 (Asked how \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effective)\par \par \uc2 "I won't say anything specific on the matter but we are conducting various simulations."\par \par \uc2 BANK OF JAPAN GOVERNOR MASAAKI SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 9, in parliament\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ's monetary easing at the (Aug. 30) emergency meeting was not aimed at \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock market volatility."\par \par \uc2 NODA, Sept. 8, in parliament\par \par \uc2 "Basically it's important to closely communicate with the international community and we are currently making efforts on this. In the end, we will take decisive measures including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when needed."\par \par \uc2 SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 8, in parliament\par \par \uc2 "I am closely communicating with my G20 counterparts at both individual and multilateral levels.\par \par \uc2 "We are poised to take additional steps if the economy turns worse than expected and downside economic risks become visible."\par \par \uc2 SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 7, in news conference\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates fluctuate on a daily basis due to various factors. It is not appropriate to determine if our policy actions were a success or not by short-term market moves alone.\par \par \uc2 "We are fully aware that export-related companies are considerably affected by the yen's recent rise.\par \par \uc2 "But monetary authorities are unable to control \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates freely ... We are carefully watching how the yen's rise impacts the Japanese economy."\par \par \uc2 NODA, Sept. 4, in TV show\par \par \uc2 "What they (Prime Minister Naoto Kan and ruling party leadership candidate Ichiro Ozawa) have been saying means the same thing. The issue is whether we would actually decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the end.\par \par \uc2 "Our statement that we will take decisive steps when needed says it all."\par \par \uc2 PRIME MINISTER NAOTO KAN, Sept. 2, in ruling party debate\par \par \uc2 "As (Federal Reserve Chairman Ben) Bernanke said, the U.S. economy has not recovered as much as had been hoped, and in a way the dollar's weakness is behind the yen's rise."\par \par \uc2 He said he had had a sense of crisis about the yen's rise for some time and so the Bank of Japan and the government acted together on policy.\par \par \uc2 DEPUTY FINANCE MINISTER MOTOHISA IKEDA, Aug. 31, in symposium\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the prerogative of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the BOJ is its agent ... It would be no good if the BOJ absorbs money from the market in such a case and I'd want the BOJ to carry out unsterilised (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )."\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not rule out cutting its policy rate to zero from the current 0.1 percent in case unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was carried out.\par \par \uc2 NODA, Aug. 31, to reporters\par \par \uc2 "I appreciate that the BOJ responded appropriately and swiftly to underlying changes in the economic and financial situation ... I expect government (stimulus) steps, coupled with the BOJ's monetary policy, to have an effect from now on.\par \par \uc2 "Current moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are one-sided. Excessive and disorderly moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market could badly affect economic and financial stability. From this standpoint, I'll closely watch market moves with great interest and take decisive steps when necessary."\par \par \uc2 SHIRAKAWA, Aug. 30, in news conference\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ will act appropriately and in a timely manner, taking into account economic and price developments as well as changes in market moves.\par \par \uc2 "There are risks to the outlook, so we cannot rule out revising down our economic scenario in the future." (Reporting by Rie Ishiguro; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/YEN-REMARKS (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100909e699000fl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
