\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dlr/yen slips towards 15-yr low, Aussie jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 850 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 08:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 (Corrects paragraph 3 to long on the dollar, not yen, and paragraph 4 to bought the dollar, not the yen. Corrects table at the bottom of story to update U.S. closing values.)\par \par \uc2 * Dollar/yen near 15-year low, seen vulnerable\par \par \uc2 * Aussie hits 4-month high on solid jobs data\par \par \uc2 * Threat of immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen tapering off\par \par \uc2 By Hideyuki Sano\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 9 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped towards a 15-year low against the yen on Thursday as traders bet that Japanese authorities are not yet ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Australian dollar hit a four-month high against the U.S. dollar on solid Australian jobs data.\par \par \uc2 The rise in the Aussie did not give its usual fillip to the U.S. dollar against the yen, via trade in the crosses, reinforcing bearish views on dollar/yen.\par \par \uc2 Traders said there had been speculation that Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be imminent after talk swirled in the market late on Wednesday that Japanese authorities had checked rates, prompting short-term players to go long on the dollar.\par \par \uc2 But wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is tapering off as nothing has happened up to now, and those who bought the dollar might be unwinding their positions, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said on Thursday that the ministry was conducting simulations on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a possible reference to the rate checks, but the yen hardly budged as the perception remains that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the dollar falls near 80 yen.\par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped 0.1 percent on the day to 83.78 yen, closing in on a 15-year low of 83.34 yen struck on the EBS platform on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 WARINESS ABOUT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped to push the dollar up briefly in early trade but it failed to sustain a rise above 84 yen, its five-day moving average.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar really seems under pressure. There's fear of a 'Japanisation' of the U.S. economy, where growth would stagnate and interest rates fall," said Koichi Yoshikawa, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shrinking yield gaps between the yen and the dollar have been a major driver behind the dollar's fall versus the yen since May.\par \par \uc2 U.S. bond yields fell on Wednesday even as Wall Street shares rose on positive news from Europe, showing that many investors are still not ready to embrace risk and putting pressure on the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Japanese government data indicated that Japanese investors bought a net 731 billion yen ($8.72 billion) of foreign bonds last week, showing no signs of repatriation by Japanese investors ahead of their half-year book-closing on Sept. 30.\par \par \uc2 Some market players are now looking to the Japanese ruling party's leadership vote next Tuesday, with Prime Minister Naoto Kan holding only a slim lead over rival Ichiro Ozawa, seen by markets as likely to pursue more reflationist policies.\par \par \uc2 If Ozawa wins the vote and becomes prime minister, some market players have said there is likely to be a knee-jerk fall in the yen.\par \par \uc2 The greenback seems to have some support at the lower end of its Bollinger Band around 83.35, said Teppei Ino, analyst at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ, noting that the dollar rebounded at that level on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Many traders think it is only a matter of time, however, before the dollar falls below that level.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index has repeatedly failed to break above its 55-day moving average, making the case for more weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DIVERGENCE?\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar jumped to a four-month high of $0.9237 after strong Australian jobs data, breaking above the $0.92 resistance it had been struggling with.\par \par \uc2 The data boosted expectations that Australia will raise rates in the future, with the OIS pricing in one more rate hike within a year.\par \par \uc2 The Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also hit a record high against the euro of A$1.3795 per euro.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar also kept Wednesday's hefty gains following a rate hike by the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It stood at C$1.0380 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The direction of monetary policy is completely the opposite between the United States and countries like Australia and Canada. So \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Aussie and the Canadian dollar will tend to be favoured," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 ' Yoshikawa.\par \par \uc2 The euro stood at $1.2730, after rising about 0.3 percent on Wednesday as Portugal raised 1.04 billion euros, helping to soothe fears about government funding in Europe. Poland's sale of five-year bonds also saw solid demand.\par \par \uc2 Later on Thursday, the Bank of England will hold a monetary policy meeting, where it is expected to keep rates on hold at 0.5 percent and to refrain from increasing its asset purchase programme.\par \par \uc2 The pound traded at $1.5460, off a 1-\u189\'00\'BD month low of $1.5296 hit on Tuesday. ($1=83.86 Yen) (Editing by Edmund Klamann)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) (CORRECTED)|LANGEN|GNN|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100909e699000bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
