\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 8\b0\par\par\uc2 1,188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2010\par 09:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS UP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WARNING AS YEN SURGES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister made it clear Wednesday the government will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tame the yen's rises if deemed necessary, but investors brushed aside his strongest warning to date and pushed the yen to a 15-year high. (published 0543 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ LEAVES ECONOMIC ASSESSMENT UNCHANGED IN SEPT REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan said the nation's economy "shows further signs of moderate recovery" in September, keeping its assessment unchanged for the fourth straight month since upgrading it in May. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA RAMPS UP JAPAN GOVERNMENT BOND BUYING IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China ramped up its purchases of Japanese government bonds in July, likely adding to speculation that the growing money flow could be contributing to the yen's recent strength and lower government bond yields. (published 0324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOVERNOR: HAVE BEEN SUPPLYING AMPLE FUNDS TO FINANCIAL FIRMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Wednesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been pumping adequate funds into the market, suggesting he doesn't think the BOJ needs to take more easing measures anytime soon. (published 0129 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA SWAN: INDEPENDENTS PART OF MINING TAX TALKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Treasurer Wayne Swan said Wednesday the non-party lawmakers who helped the Labor Party secure another term in office will be involved in talks on the final design of a controversial plan to tax the profits of mining companies. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RATES PAUSE PUTS CUSHION UNDER AUSTRALIAN HOUSE LENDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A recent downturn in lending for Australian housing is bottoming out as a lengthening pause in interest rate hikes puts a cushion under the sector. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA'S BROAD MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH IN JULY SLOWEST IN 11 MONTHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in South Korea's broadest measure of money supply continued to slow in July, posting its weakest gain in 11 months, Bank of Korea data showed Wednesday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: ASIAN RESERVES UP IN AUG AS CENTRAL BANKS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves hit a new all-time high in August, according to Dow Jones Newswires calculations, driven by strong inflows attracted by the region's growth rates and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to contain local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: VODAFONE SELLS CHINA MOBILE STAKE FOR GBP4.3 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vodafone Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the world's biggest mobile operator by revenue, said late Tuesday it sold its 3.2% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Mobile Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for GBP4.3 billion before tax and transaction costs, the first of many expected minority shareholding divestments. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GIC IN ADVANCED TALKS TO BUY 15% STAKE IN BRAZIL'S BTG PACTUAL - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  is in advanced talks to buy an around 15% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco BTG Pactual SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , one of Brazil's top investment banks, for about US$2.4 billion, a person familiar with the talks said Wednesday. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOSTER'S REJECTED A$2.3B-A$2.7B PRIVATE EQUITY OFFER FOR WINE BUSINESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foster's Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has rejected a cash offer for its wine business from a private equity firm, which valued the unit at A$2.3 billion-A$2.7 billion, and instead is pushing ahead with a demerger of its beer and wine divisions. (published 2255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =CHINA MING YANG WIND POWER FILES IPO FOR $400 MLN ADS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Ming Yang Wind Power Group Ltd. filed plans to hold an initial public offering of up to about $400 million American depositary shares, with the wind turbine manufacturer planning to use the proceeds to expand production capacity and for research and development. (published 2159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHANGFENG AXLE SEEKING TO RAISE UP TO US$115 MLN IN HK IPO - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Automotive parts maker Changfeng Axle Co. is seeking to raise up to US$115 million in a Hong Kong initial public offering later this month, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Wednesday. (published 0146 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MIRABELA NICKEL IN PLACEMENT TO RAISE UP TO US$165 MILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazilian-focused miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mirabela Nickel Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . launched a share placement Wednesday to raise US$135 million-US$165 million to pay down debt, fund working capital, and assist in the expansion of its Santa Rita project. (published 2353 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA SELECTS THREE FIRMS TO MANAGE WOORI FINANCE SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government Wednesday announced \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Securities Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Securities Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will manage the sale of its 57% stake in Woori Finance Holdings Co., currently valued at KRW6 trillion --a move that will push forward the privatization of the country's largest financial holding company by assets. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VAYUPAK FUND PLANS TO SUBSCRIBE TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 THAI AIRWAYS\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' NEW SHARES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Vayupak Fund is planning to participate in the upcoming share offering of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai Airways International PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , most of which will be allotted to existing shareholders and a handful to general investors, a co-manager of the fund said Wednesday. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: ITI CHAIRMAN SAYS SOUGHT INR3.50 BLN MORE AID FROM GOVERNMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ITI Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has sought an additional INR3.50 billion in financial aid from the Indian government as the state-run telecommunications equipment maker seeks to upgrade its plant infrastructure and turn profitable by fiscal year 2012. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES DROP; YEN STRENGTH HURTS JAPAN EXPORTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower Wednesday after Wall Street declined amid concerns over the health of European banks, with the region's financial stocks getting hit, while exporter shares dragged the Tokyo market lower as the yen touched a fresh 15-year high against the U.S. dollar. (published 0415 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: 2 MISSING AFTER OIL PLATFORM ACCIDENT IN EAST CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More than 30 workers trapped on an offshore oil platform badly listing in the East China Sea were rescued Wednesday morning but two remain missing, authorities said. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  = \par =REFINERY WATCH: JAPAN TO CUT OCT RUNS; 18% OF CAPACITY OFFLINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan is likely to cut its crude processing volume in October from the previous month as at least 18% of its crude oil refining capacity will go offline for planned maintenance or wind back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PETROCHINA FUSHUN EXPLOSION HAS NO IMPACT ON REFINERY -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An explosion at \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . unit \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fushun Petrochemical Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in northern China's Liaoning province hasn't impacted its crude oil refinery or ethylene facility, as they are located far apart, a media official at Fushun Petrochemical said Wednesday. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA CORN PRICES LARGELY STABLE ON AMPLE STOCKS;HARVEST AHEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corn prices in China's major producing areas stayed largely flat in the week to Wednesday, with downstream processors' stocks built up due to recent government reserve auctions. (published 0259 GMT) [ 08-09-10 0704GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100908e698000kh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
