 INDEPENDENTS PART OF MINING TAX TALKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Treasurer Wayne Swan said Wednesday the non-party lawmakers who helped the Labor Party secure another term in office will be involved in talks on the final design of a controversial plan to tax the profits of mining companies. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: RATES PAUSE PUTS CUSHION UNDER AUSTRALIAN HOUSE LENDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A recent downturn in lending for Australian housing is bottoming out as a lengthening pause in interest rate hikes puts a cushion under the sector. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA'S BROAD MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH IN JULY SLOWEST IN 11 MONTHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in South Korea's broadest measure of money supply continued to slow in July, posting its weakest gain in 11 months, Bank of Korea data showed Wednesday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INFOTEL BROADBAND SERVICES RAISES INR10 BLN VIA BONDS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's Infotel Broadband Services Ltd., a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., has raised INR10 billion via bonds, a person familiar with the matter said. (published 0436 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: ASIAN RESERVES UP IN AUG AS CENTRAL BANKS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves hit a new all-time high in August, according to Dow Jones Newswires calculations, driven by strong inflows attracted by the region's growth rates and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to contain local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation. (published 03