\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Portugal Bond Sale Lifts Euro Against Dollar, Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew J. Johnson   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2010\par 22:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The euro rose against the dollar and yen Wednesday after a euro-zone government debt auction soothed investor nerves, leading them into higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The successful auction of Portuguese government debt overshadowed concerns about the credibility of European bank stress tests. The euro had fallen Tuesday on a Wall Street Journal report that European bank stress tests underestimated the exposure of some major banks to sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2 "The successful Portuguese bond auction shows that while European markets have tightened, they do remain open," said Lena Komileva, head of G7 market economics at Tullett Prebon in London. "They are not frozen."\par \par \uc2 To see the euro's performance against the dollar, please see:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4563"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4563}}}\par \par \uc2 As investors rode the wave of positive sentiment to send U.S. stocks higher, the dollar rebounded from an overnight 15-year low against the yen.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday afternoon, the euro was at $1.2716 after hitting an intraday high of $1.2764, compared with $1.2689 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y83.92 compared with Y83.80, after falling as low as Y83.34 overnight. The euro was at Y106.72, up from Y106.33. The U.K. pound was at $1.5465, up from $1.5350. The dollar was at CHF1.0122 compared with CHF1.0098.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 82.608 compared with 82.815.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar gained sharply against the greenback after the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  raised interest rates, its third-consecutive increase of key rates.\par \par \uc2 "It's partially a return of risk appetite," said Andrew Chaveriat, technical \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in New York of Wednesday's move higher in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely tied to global growth, such as the Australian and New Zealand dollars.\par \par \uc2 Until new U.S. economic data emerge, investors would likely keep the dollar itself range-bound, said John Doyle, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Tempus Consulting in Washington. "We would expect the euro to trade within $1.2650 and $1.2850," he said.\par \par \uc2 Japan Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda was the latest official to warn markets that Japan was ready to act to bolster the yen, specifically raising the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time.\par \par \uc2 "We will take decisive steps--which of course include \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 --when it becomes necessary," Noda said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have said the comments showed greater seriousness among \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities toward the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , something they haven't done since 2004. But there is still skepticism as to whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would actually happen.\par \par \uc2 "Traders are not buying it," said Doyle of Tempus Consulting, referring to imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many believe there will be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  until at least Sept. 14, when the leadership of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruling party is decided, according to Hidetoshi Yanagihara, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 , meanwhile, delivered a cautious tone as it announced its 25-basis-point rate increase, saying, "Any further reduction in monetary policy stimulus would need to be carefully considered in light of the unusual uncertainty surrounding the outlook."\par \par \uc2 The rate increase puts the bank's overnight target rate at 1.00%. In June, the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  became the first \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Group of Seven leading nations to raise interest rates since the global economic crisis took hold two years ago.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was at C$1.0373 in afternoon New York trading, down from C$1.0490 just before the rate announcement. It was at C$1.0475 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 With the ICE Dollar Index weakening, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bearish exchange-traded fund was up 0.27% from late Tuesday, while its PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bullish was down 0.33%. The two exchange-traded funds are based on \uc2 Deutsche Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures indexes, whose composition mirrors that of the ICE's Dollar Index.\par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Johnson, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3092; andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Bradley Davis in New York, Karen Johnson in Toronto and Kosaku Narioka in Tokyo contributed to this article.) [ 09-08-10 1623ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100908e698000go\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
