\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:Taiwan Aug Econ Data Show Fundamentals Strong-Macq\b0\par\par\uc2 1,514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2010\par 06:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0447 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan August economic data (CPI, Exports) indicate economic fundamentals remain strong, but growth momentum moderating, stabilizing to sustainable rates from record pace between 2H 2009 and 1H 2010, says Macquarie. "Price and monetary indicators show still-tepid inflation and abundant market liquidity. We expect the CBC (Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) to continue its gradual withdrawal of monetary stimulus with another 12.5 basis point rate hike," house adds.(paul.mozur@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0444 GMT [Dow Jones] Investors continue to avoid Singapore shares after early selloff, with STI surrendering almost all its 1.1% gain so far this week. Index off 1.0% at 3006.79 midday. If 3000 gives way for rest of session, next support expected at Friday's 2977 intraday low. Market breadth slightly negative, with overall volume thin at 673.4 million shares worth S$545.8 million. Small caps, penny shares fare better than blue chips, with FTSE ST Small Cap Index +0.3%, FTSE ST Catalist Index +2.4%. "Traders are zooming in on the lower liners and avoiding the large caps. The overall pullback is not too bad, but the market clearly needs fresh leads to bring it back up and push it higher," says local house trader. Lower liners in play include \uc2 China Hongxing Sports\uc2  (BR9.SG), +8.1% at S$0.20, Hisaka (FV2.SG), +12.9% at S$0.35, Z-Obee (D5N.SG), +3.8% at S$0.41, Biosensors (B20.SG), +2.4% at S$0.86. (frankie.ho@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0443 GMT [Dow Jones] KLCI down 0.3% at 1430.01 midday, tracking declines in U.S., regional stocks; investors also taking profit ahead of long-weekend, dealers say. "We believe the current consolidation will likely continue for the rest of the week," RHB Research says; pegs support at 1422 (10-day moving average), resistance at 1441 (2010 high). Financial markets will be closed from midday tomorrow for Idul Fitri, will re-open Monday. Among decliners, Top Glove (7113.KU) down 3.9% at MYR5.61, \uc2 MMC Corp\uc2  (2194.KU) down 2.5% at MYR2.71, AMMB (1015.KU) down 1.7% at MYR5.83; among gainers, Plenitude (5075.KU) +10.3% at MYR4.28 after announcing 1-for-1 bonus issue, Bina Puri (5932.KU) +5.3% at MYR1.19 after unveiling MYR500 million mall project. (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0440 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares end down 0.5% at 458.44 as local retailers continue to take profits after key index +8.2% over past 7 sessions. "Some blue chips are still up by more than 10% month-to-date," says trader. Tips strong technical support at 450; thinks local institutions, foreigners may buy amid growing expectations government will soon come up with measures that will help boost cash flows. State media reported yesterday money supply as of end-August rose 13% from end of last year, but lower than government forecast of 20% rise. Volume moderate with 56 million shares valued at VND1.48 trillion exchanging hands. Among most active, SSI (SSI.VH) ends down 2.4% at VND28,500 after rising 12.6% over past 7 sessions, Investment & Trading of Real Eastate JSC (ITC.VH) down 0.4% at VND25,700 after 19.5% rise over same period. REE (REE.VH) end down 2.3% at VND17,100 after gaining 10.3% over same period. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0434 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/HKD higher as local banks cover short positions, while weak local stocks lend support, says senior trader at Singapore bank. HSI last down 1.4%. Tips pair in 7.7700-7.7730 band near-term. Players turn risk averse, thus supporting USD, "but I've spotted a U.S. 