\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Slips; Noda Fails To Stop Yen's Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Hastings   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 777 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2010\par 11:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The euro came under renewed selling pressure Wednesday as worries about European banks and the threat of sovereign default returned to financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Despite a warning from the Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains possible, the yen pushed to a new 15-year high against the dollar as investors returned to safe havens.\par \par \uc2 The pound also found some support as the latest measure of U.K. house prices came in stronger than expected and new merger and acquisition flows worked in its favor.\par \par \uc2 Euro bulls have been frustrated over the last day or so by weak German industrial orders data that indicate the euro zone's largest and strongest economy is starting to slow.\par \par \uc2 This has combined with more reports that European banks are more exposed than expected and more speculation that they may yet have to seek more capital.\par \par \uc2 "The debt crisis is more likely to return to the center of attention," said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy team at \uc2 Commerzbank AG\uc2 , noting that the price of credit default swaps on problem countries have risen "considerably" since early August and are now not far from their peaks.\par \par \uc2 As investors moved out of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and back into safe havens, the euro fell to a new all-time low of CHF1.2765.\par \par \uc2 See the euro's fall against the Swiss franc:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4560"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4560}}}\par \par \uc2 The yen was also a major gainer, with the dollar tumbling to a 15-year low at Y83.34.\par \par \uc2 The strong-yen trend was helped by data showing that Japanese machinery orders rose 8.8% in July, rather than just 2.0% as expected.\par \par \uc2 The yen's rally came, however, after Finance Minister Noda appeared keen to send an unequivocal message to the market that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains possible. Other officials, including ones from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had suggested over the last few days that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't imminent.\par \par \uc2 Although Noda's warning had a brief impact on sentiment, the yen soon resumed its advance on the market assumption that any attempt to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be successful unless the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  eases monetary policy at the same time.\par \par \uc2 Hans Redeker, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 BNP Paribas SA\uc2  in London, pointed to the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  failure to hold the Swiss franc back with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May for just this reason.\par \par \uc2 "Hence, the market will pay more attention to Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa's comment compared to talk coming out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Redeker said, noting that Shirakawa has recently noted that quantitative easing was helpful in stabilizing financial markets but had little supportive impact on the economy.\par \par \uc2 Sterling managed to find support despite the general move into safe havens, rising nearly a full cent as Vodaphone PLC puts its stake in China Mobile up for sale for about GBP4 billion.\par \par \uc2 Additional help for the pound came from Halifax house price data, which defied expectations of a decline, to show a 0.2% rise last month. However, sterling backed off a little from its earlier highs after new industrial production data showed a 0.3% increase in July, not quite as much as the 0.5% rise that had been forecast.\par \par \uc2 By midmorning, the euro was down at $1.2683 from $1.2689 late Tuesday in New York, according to EBS. It was also down at Y106.21 from Y106.33 while after an early decline to Y83.34, the dollar managed to recover to Y83.74, compared with Y83.80.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was hardly changed at CHF1.0083 from CHF1.0098, while the pound rallied to $1.5441 from $1.5350.\par \par \uc2 Although depressed risk sentiment is likely to prevail, as European woes dominate the market's mood, there could be some relief later in the day if the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  surprises the market with a rate hike or if the latest U.S. Beige Book gives a more upbeat assessment of the U.S. economy than analysts have been anticipating.\par \par \uc2 -By Nicholas Hastings, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9493; nick.hastings@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 08-09-10 0934GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100908e698000vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
