\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 925 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 10:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE PRIVATE SECTOR GROWTH EASES IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone private sector growth slowed slightly in August, but employment rose at the fastest rate for more than two years with jobs added in Germany, France, and Italy, the final results of a monthly survey by Markit showed Friday. (published 0825 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB WELLINK: 'IRRELEVANT' IF WORLD ECONOMY SEES SMALL 'DOUBLE DIP' IN NEAR TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council member Nout Wellink said Friday it is "irrelevant" if the world economy undergoes a mild second recession in the near term, adding that he is most concerned about the longer term challenges of economic restructuring. (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF YEN RISE GRADUAL - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would find it hard to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the yen's rise is gradual, but the authorities are more determined than ever to act against any unusually rapid exchange-rate moves, people familiar with the matter said. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF SURVEY BODES WELL FOR GDP; ILL FOR OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Capital spending by Japanese businesses slipped in the April-June quarter, but inventory investment surged, suggesting the government will revise upward its initial gross domestic product growth estimate for the second quarter next week. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FSB DRAGHI: TO HAVE FINAL RECOMMENDATIONS ON BANK LIQUIDITY, CAPITAL REQUIREMENTS BY NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Final proposals for banks' capital and liquidity requirements will be ready in time for the November Group of 20 leaders summit, Financial Stability Board Chairman Mario Draghi said Friday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOE TUCKER: PROGRESS MADE ON NEW BANK CAPITAL RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of England Deputy Governor Paul Tucker said Friday that the Financial Stability Board and the Basel Committee for Banking Supervision are making "substantive progress" on devising new capital and liquidity requirements for banks, "notwithstanding what has been in the press." (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH PM SUPPORTS LABOR MINISTER WOERTH, SLAMS "SMEAR CAMPAIGN" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French Labor Minister Eric Woerth will remain in the government to see a crucial pensions reform through parliament, the French prime minister said in a statement released by his office Thursday night. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALIAN HEAD OF STATE CALLS FOR NEW INDUSTRIAL POLICY-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian President Giorgio Napolitano called on the government to adopt a "serious industrial policy" and to fill the post of industry minister which became vacant four months ago after a resignation, Italian newspapers reported Friday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC-AFFILIATED SCHOLAR: CHINA COULD CONSIDER WIDER YUAN BAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China could consider widening the yuan's trading band further to increase the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's flexibility and allow market forces to play a greater role in determining the exchange rate, a scholar affiliated with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wrote in a column published Friday in the state-run Shanghai Securities News. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PERFORMANCE OF SERVICES INDEX UP 0.9 PTS IN AUGUST VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's services sector was sluggish in August as political uncertainty and the steady withdrawal of fiscal stimulus damped activity. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA INDEPENDENT KATTER HINTS AT SUPPORT FOR LABOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian independent lawmaker Bob Katter Friday said he is not opposed to backing a Labor government and hinted at room to compromise on his policy demands, delivering another boost to Prime Minister Julia Gillard as she seeks to form a minority government. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: THE SWISS FRANC HAS MUCH FURTHER TO RUN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Swiss franc really is the new Deutsche mark, then the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could have a lot further to run, especially against the euro. (published 0720 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOCUS: JAPAN'S POLITICAL TURMOIL ADDS TO JGB MARKET JITTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An unfolding political saga that could lead to a new prime minister who strongly favors higher fiscal spending has taken Japan's already jittery government bond market by surprise, sending prices on a roller-coaster ride. (published 0724 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR/USD POISED FOR MORE GAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Consolidates beneath Wednesday's high at 1.2856, but bulls have regained control of the near-term to threaten a break through 1.2856. The August 18 lower high at 1.2923 lies in wait on a sustained break, which is close to a 1.618 extension target at 1.2936. Thursday's low at 1.2776 will limit corrective weakness, and only below there would concern bulls, exposing 1.2740. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BONDS TO LOSE MORE GROUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: The near-term bear trend extended Thursday to confirm an evening star reversal pattern and support at 132.44 is braced for renewed pressure. Thursday's high at 133.43 marked the peak of a bear flag/wedge and a third day of weakness is likely towards the 131.64 area. Regaining ground above 132.95 is required to provide respite, and create room for a recovery toward the 133.43 high. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: AUSTRALIA'S RBA TO SIT PAT, YET OUTLOOK ANYTHING BUT CLEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  will leave interest rates unchanged at its regular monthly board meeting Tuesday citing a still uncertain global backdrop and its ongoing satisfaction with the fact lending rates across the economy are back at "average" levels, according to economists. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MONEY TALKS: VIETNAM LIKELY TO WEAKEN DONG AGAIN TO SPUR EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflationary pressures could soon re-emerge in Vietnam--but that's not likely to stop the growth-focused government from devaluing the dong again, possibly before year-end. (published 0305 GMT) [ 03-09-10 0856GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100903e693000k4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
