\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 3\b0\par\par\uc2 1,825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF YEN RISE GRADUAL - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would find it hard to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the yen's rise is gradual, but the authorities are more determined than ever to act against any unusually rapid exchange-rate moves, people familiar with the matter said. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN MOF SURVEY BODES WELL FOR GDP; ILL FOR OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Capital spending by Japanese businesses slipped in the April-June quarter, but inventory investment surged, suggesting the government will revise upward its initial gross domestic product growth estimate for the second quarter next week. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  =2ND UPDATE: SOUTH KOREA REVISED 2Q GDP UP 1.4% ON QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economy grew for the sixth straight quarter in the three months to June, stoking calls for continued rate hikes to rein in rising inflationary pressures. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AFTER SINGAPORE DOLLAR HITS RECORD HIGH -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday after the Singapore dollar hit an all-time high against the greenback, a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOT: READY TO IMPOSE ADDITIONAL MEASURES IF NEEDED TO CURB BAHT RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  is ready to impose additional measures if needed to curb the baht's rise, Senior Director Wongwatoo Potirat said Friday. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  =UPDATE: HK MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY EXPANDS FOR 13TH MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's manufacturing activity expanded for the 13th consecutive month in August, reflecting continued strength in demand from mainland China and an improving local labor market, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0603 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES WPI UP 1.4% TO 312.5 IN WEEK TO AUG 21 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wholesale price index for primary articles in India rose 1.4% to 312.5 in the week to Aug. 21, from a provisional 308.1 in the previous week, according to data issued Friday by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PERFORMANCE OF SERVICES INDEX UP 0.9 PTS IN AUGUST VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's services sector was sluggish in August as political uncertainty and the steady withdrawal of fiscal stimulus damped activity. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA GAS PLANS TO RAISE $300 MLN VIA OCTOBER BOND ISSUE -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Gas Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to raise $300 million by issuing Swiss franc-denominated bonds in October to fund its overseas \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a company official said Friday. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB WELLINK: 'IRRELEVANT' IF WORLD ECONOMY SEES SMALL 'DOUBLE DIP' IN NEAR TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council member Nout Wellink said Friday it is "irrelevant" if the world economy undergoes a mild second recession in the near term, adding that he is most concerned about the longer term challenges of economic restructuring. (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BOE TUCKER: PROGRESS MADE ON NEW BANK CAPITAL RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The two bodies are aiming to prepare a final list of conditions for banks to comply with by the time of a meeting of Group of 20 heads of government in November, a goal that some observers have said may not be realistic. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FSB DRAGHI: TO HAVE FINAL RECOMMENDATIONS ON BANK LIQUIDITY, CAPITAL REQUIREMENTS BY NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Final proposals for banks' capital and liquidity requirements will be ready in time for the November Group of 20 leaders summit, Financial Stability Board Chairman Mario Draghi said on Friday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA INDEPENDENT KATTER HINTS AT SUPPORT FOR LABOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian independent lawmaker Bob Katter Friday said he is not opposed to backing a Labor government and hinted at room to compromise on his policy demands, delivering another boost to Prime Minister Julia Gillard as she seeks to form a minority government. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: VIETNAM LIKELY TO WEAKEN DONG AGAIN TO SPUR EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflationary pressures could soon re-emerge in Vietnam--but that's not likely to stop the growth-focused government from devaluing the dong again, possibly before year-end. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: AUSTRALIA'S RBA TO SIT PAT, YET OUTLOOK ANYTHING BUT CLEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  will leave interest rates unchanged at its regular monthly board meeting Tuesday citing a still uncertain global backdrop and its ongoing satisfaction with the fact lending rates across the economy are back at "average" levels, according to economists. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: PHILIPPINES AUGUST INFLATION LIKELY STEADY AT 3.9% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Annual inflation in the Philippines in August likely remained at 3.9% as softer oil prices might have cushioned price pressures arising from robust economic growth. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NINGBO PORT TO START ROADSHOW FOR SHANGHAI IPO MONDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ningbo Port Co., a major port operator in eastern China, said Friday it will launch a four-day roadshow Monday for its initial public offering ahead of a planned Shanghai listing. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =CHINA VANKE AUG PROPERTY SALES MORE THAN DOUBLE TO CNY11.99B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Vanke Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said its property sales in August more than doubled from a year earlier to CNY11.99 billion, a record monthly performance for a Chinese property developer. (published 2328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: FORTESCUE DENIES CLAIM IT'S BREACHED LEUCADIA FUNDING PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fortescue Metals Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Friday denied accusations by shareholder \f28 \uc2 \f2 Leucadia National Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . that it breached a funding agreement with its long-time partner, which is suing the iron ore miner for what it views as an "extraordinary" attempt to raise cheap funding at its expense. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALLIED FARMER: MANAGING DIRECTOR ALLOWAY STEPS DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rural services company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Allied Farmers Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that Managing Director \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rob Alloway\f28 \uc2 \f2  would step down from this role in December. (published 2358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SLATER & GORDON EXPECTS TO TAKE ACTION AGAINST NUFARM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Law firm Slater & Gordon said Friday it will mount a class action against crop chemical company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nufarm Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in response to shareholder requests after a shock profit downgrade that saw the company halve its underlying net profit guidance in July. (published 0122 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: TOSHIBA TO LAUNCH NEW TABLET AS IPAD DRIVES MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toshiba Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it will release by year-end a tablet computer that runs on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Android operating system, as the Japanese electronics maker aims to grab a chunk of a fast-growing tablet device market spearheaded by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s iPad. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PTT EXPECTS 2H REVENUE LIKELY ABOVE 1H AFTER MAP TA PHUT RULING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PTT PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's largest energy conglomerate by revenue, said Friday that its second-half revenue is likely to improve from the first half after a court allowed its sixth gas-separation plant to go ahead. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SIAM CEMENT: MOST MAP TA PHUT PROJECTS CAN PROCEED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Siam Cement PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday that most of its industrial projects at a controversial industrial estate can continue following a legal ruling. (published 0208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: TPG SELLS REMAINING STAKE IN \f28 \uc2 \f2 PING AN INSURANCE\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; RAISES US$1.16 BLN - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Private-equity firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 TPG Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has sold its remaining stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ping An Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . of China Ltd. for US$1.16 billion, a person familiar with the situation said Friday, in the latest example of how the U.S. company is reaping sizable profits by exiting some of its investments in Asia. (published 0521 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: TATA CONSULTANCY UNIT DILIGENTA EYES 2 CONTRACTS WORTH OVER GBP100 MLN EACH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Diligenta Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Consultancy Services Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., has been approached by two prospective clients for outsourcing contracts worth more than GBP100 million each, a senior executive said. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIGMA PHARMACEUTICALS\f28 \uc2 \f2  MAY FACE SHAREHOLDER CLASS ACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sigma Pharmaceuticals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it may face a shareholder class action alleging it failed to disclose information required under Australian corporations laws ahead of its A$297 million equity raising last year. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ADARO ENERGY OFFICIAL: IN TALKS TO ACQUIRE STAKE IN BHAKTI ENERGI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Adaro Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday that it is in talks with shareholders of PT Bhakti Energi to buy a stake in the unlisted coal miner, Adaro's spokesman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Andre Mamuaya\f28 \uc2 \f2  told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MURLI INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  DROPS PLAN TO SELL STAKE IN CEMENT PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Murli Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has dropped plans to sell a stake in its Chandrapur cement plant in the western state of Maharashtra, and will instead use other means to raise up to INR10 billion to finance its future cement and power projects. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MAYBANK LOOKING TO GROW ISLAMIC FINANCING TO 33% OF MALAYSIAN OPS BY 2015 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malayan Banking Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Maybank, is looking to grow the Islamic component of its financing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Malaysia to 33% by 2015 from the current 24%, the bank's chief executive and president, Abdul Wahid Omar, said Friday. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY HIGHER; TECHS LEAD IN TOKYO, SEOUL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Friday with technology plays leading gains in Tokyo and Seoul, while weakness in China's banking stocks dragged the Shanghai market lower. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PTT EXPECTS 2H REVENUE LIKELY ABOVE 1H AFTER MAP TA PHUT RULING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-09-10 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PTT PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's largest energy conglomerate by revenue, said Friday that its second-half revenue is likely to improve from the first half after a court allowed its sixth gas-separation plant to go ahead. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ABOITIZ POWER\f28 \uc2 \f2  MULLS $2.8 BLN, 1,400-MW CAPACITY EXPANSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aboitiz Power Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to expand its capacity by as much as 1,400 megawatts in the coming years, a move that could require $2.8 billion in new investment, company President and Chief Executive Erramon Aboitiz said. (published 0128 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: FORTESCUE DENIES CLAIM IT'S BREACHED LEUCADIA FUNDING PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fortescue Metals Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Friday denied accusations by shareholder \f28 \uc2 \f2 Leucadia National Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . that it breached a funding agreement with its long-time partner, which is suing the iron ore miner for what it views as an "extraordinary" attempt to raise cheap funding at its expense. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI CUP LUMP PRICES HIGH; RAINS DISRUPT LATEX PRODUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cup lump--or coagulated field latex--prices in Thailand have increased about 15% since early June to trade above THB100 a kilogram, as rains disrupt production and demand for block rubber grades rises, said traders. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLDEN AGRI: GOLDEN VEROLEUM, LIBERIA GOVT IN PALM OIL PLANTATION PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Golden Agri-Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that Golden VerOleum Inc., in which the palm oil grower has an equity stake through investment in a fund, has tied up with the Liberian government to plant oil palms in the African nation. (published 0058 GMT) [ 03-09-10 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100903e693000f5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
