\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 08:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF YEN RISE GRADUAL - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would find it hard to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the yen's rise is gradual, but the authorities are more determined than ever to act against any unusually rapid exchange-rate moves, people familiar with the matter said. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN MOF SURVEY BODES WELL FOR GDP; ILL FOR OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Capital spending by Japanese businesses slipped in the April-June quarter, but inventory investment surged, suggesting the government will revise upward its initial gross domestic product growth estimate for the second quarter next week. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: SOUTH KOREA REVISED 2Q GDP UP 1.4% ON QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economy grew for the sixth straight quarter in the three months to June, stoking calls for continued rate hikes to rein in rising inflationary pressures. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AFTER SINGAPORE DOLLAR HITS RECORD HIGH -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday after the Singapore dollar hit an all-time high against the greenback, a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOT: READY TO IMPOSE ADDITIONAL MEASURES IF NEEDED TO CURB BAHT RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  is ready to impose additional measures if needed to curb the baht's rise, Senior Director Wongwatoo Potirat said Friday. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC-AFFILIATED SCHOLAR: CHINA COULD CONSIDER WIDER YUAN BAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China could consider widening the yuan's trading band further to increase the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's flexibility and allow market forces to play a greater role in determining the exchange rate, a scholar affiliated with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wrote in a column published Friday in the state-run Shanghai Securities News. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: HK MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY EXPANDS FOR 13TH MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's manufacturing activity expanded for the 13th consecutive month in August, reflecting continued strength in demand from mainland China and an improving local labor market, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0603 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PERFORMANCE OF SERVICES INDEX UP 0.9 PTS IN AUGUST VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's services sector was sluggish in August as political uncertainty and the steady withdrawal of fiscal stimulus damped activity. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA GAS PLANS TO RAISE $300 MLN VIA OCTOBER BOND ISSUE -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Gas Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to raise $300 million by issuing Swiss franc-denominated bonds in October to fund its overseas \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a company official said Friday. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BOE TUCKER: PROGRESS MADE ON NEW BANK CAPITAL RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The two bodies are aiming to prepare a final list of conditions for banks to comply with by the time of a meeting of Group of 20 heads of government in November, a goal that some observers have said may not be realistic. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA TO ANNOUNCE NEW BANK RESERVE RULES AROUND 0630 GMT - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia will announce Friday new reserve requirements for commercial lenders aimed at absorbing excess liquidity while at the same time providing room for banks to lend, an official with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA INDEPENDENT KATTER HINTS AT SUPPORT FOR LABOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian independent lawmaker Bob Katter Friday said he is not opposed to backing a Labor government and hinted at room to compromise on his policy demands, delivering another boost to Prime Minister Julia Gillard as she seeks to form a minority government. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: VIETNAM LIKELY TO WEAKEN DONG AGAIN TO SPUR EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflationary pressures could soon re-emerge in Vietnam--but that's not likely to stop the growth-focused government from devaluing the dong again, possibly before year-end. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: AUSTRALIA'S RBA TO SIT PAT, YET OUTLOOK ANYTHING BUT CLEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  will leave interest rates unchanged at its regular monthly board meeting Tuesday citing a still uncertain global backdrop and its ongoing satisfaction with the fact lending rates across the economy are back at "average" levels, according to economists. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-09-10 0605GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100903e693000aq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
