\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 06:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF UNLIKELY TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF DOLLAR/YEN DECLINE GRADUAL -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government would find it hard to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the dollar declines gradually against the yen, but the authorities are more determined than ever to act against any unusually rapid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate moves, several people familiar with the matter said. (published 0220 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN MOF SURVEY BODES WELL FOR GDP; ILL FOR OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Capital spending by Japanese businesses slipped in the April-June quarter, but inventory investment surged, suggesting the government will revise upward its initial gross domestic product growth estimate for the second quarter next week. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: SOUTH KOREA REVISED 2Q GDP UP 1.4% ON QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economy grew for the sixth straight quarter in the three months to June, stoking calls for continued rate hikes to rein in rising inflationary pressures. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AFTER SINGAPORE DOLLAR HITS RECORD HIGH -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday after the Singapore dollar hit an all-time high against the greenback, a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  HK AUGUST PURCHASING MANAGERS INDEX 52.3 VS JULY 51.3 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Hong Kong Purchasing Managers Index rose to 52.3 in August from 51.3 in July, signaling a strengthening of business condition in the city, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PERFORMANCE OF SERVICES INDEX UP 0.9 PTS IN AUGUST VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's services sector was sluggish in August as political uncertainty and the steady withdrawal of fiscal stimulus damped activity. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA GAS PLANS TO RAISE $300 MLN VIA OCTOBER BOND ISSUE -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Gas Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to raise $300 million by issuing Swiss franc-denominated bonds in October to fund its overseas \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a company official said Friday. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE TUCKER: PROGRESS MADE ON CAPITAL REQUIREMENTS FOR BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of England Deputy Governor Paul Tucker said Friday that the Financial Stability Board and the Basel Committee for Banking Supervision are making "substantive progress" on devising new capital and liquidity requirements for banks, "notwithstanding what has been in the press." (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA INDEPENDENT KATTER HINTS AT SUPPORT FOR LABOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian independent lawmaker Bob Katter Friday said he is not opposed to backing a Labor government and hinted at room to compromise on his policy demands, delivering another boost to Prime Minister Julia Gillard as she seeks to form a minority government. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: VIETNAM LIKELY TO WEAKEN DONG AGAIN TO SPUR EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflationary pressures could soon re-emerge in Vietnam--but that's not likely to stop the growth-focused government from devaluing the dong again, possibly before year-end. (published 0305 GMT) [ 03-09-10 0407GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100903e69300076\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
