xpansion cycle in MSCI HK about 26 months; "currently, we are only 10 months into this cycle." House's year-end target for HSI at 26,193. Ping An +3.6% at HK$68.45 as Newbridge's stake sale viewed as lifting overhang, is best-performing blue chip; worst performer Esprit (0330.HK), slumps 5.4% to HK$40.60 in further post-results weakness. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0219 GMT [Dow Jones] Bank Negara likely to keep policy rates unchanged for remainder of year after maintaining key rate at 2.75% yesterday, says OSK Research. Following Thursday's policy decision, "we revised our year-end forecast for OPR from 3.00% to 2.75%," house says. OSK expects resumption of rate hikes in latter half of next year, possibly in 3Q. "For 2011, contingent on the global economic recovery and, subsequently, the timing of the Fed rate hike, we forecast the OPR to be raised to 3.50% by end-2011," house says. Adds, given strong growth momentum in 1H, current official forecast of 4.5%-5.5% growth may be revised higher during Budget 2011 announcement in October. OSK expects growth at 7.5% for the year. OSK also says \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  might have 8 meetings in 2011, rather than 6 they have currently set, given uncertainties in global financial markets. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0216 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares likely higher, supported by gains in most regional markets, firm IDR, traders say; tip benchmark index in 3110-3140 range today after ending down 0.4% yesterday at 3122.149. "Overall, I think the market will continue to consolidate ahead of the Bank Indonesia's policy rate meeting later today but bargain-buying by local funds may drive the main index slightly higher," says trader at Lautandhana Securities. Coal miner Bumi (BUMI.JK), palm oil producer Sampoerna Agro (SGRO.JK) may lead gains, thanks to higher commodity prices, but Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) may fall on profit-taking after recent outperformance. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0216 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD lower at 31.987 vs 32.040 at yesterday's close. Dealer from foreign bank says trading thin ahead of U.S. nonfarm payrolls data due later in day, although overall positive market sentiment lends some strength to TWD. Tips tight 31.940-32.040 band today. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again before closing; it has been actively selling TWD in market in recent months, traders believe \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to keep USD/TWD at around 32.000 so as not to hurt competitiveness of exports sector. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0215 GMT [Dow Jones] Silver slightly lower at $19.61, down 4 cents after rising 1.5% overnight, with May high of $19.81 in sight, says ScotiaMocatta. "We are bullish on silver looking for an eventual test of the 2008 high of $21.35." Adds gold/silver ratio broke lower through August low of 64.30 to current 63.72. Tips April low of 62.66 as next major support followed by 2010 low of 60.77. Silver leading gilded life, tracking gold and also getting boost when industrial metals rise, although doesn't seem to suffer when base metals fall as long as gold remains firm. (james.campbell@dowjones.com) [ 09-02-10 2246ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100903e6930001w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
