\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:EUR/USD Up On Short Covers, Model Buys;1.2850 Eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 1,440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 04:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0233 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD may rise to 1.2850, near Thursday's high, before release of U.S. non-farm payroll data for August due 1230 GMT as short-term investors cover shorts, model funds buying pair, says senior dealer at major Japan bank. But says sharper rises unlikely because ordinary investors avoid large bidding before major U.S. economic indicator. Pair last 1.2828. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0228 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP moving lower, weighed by broad USD weakness, improving global risk appetite. Pair last at 44.75, lowest in 4 months, vs 4.95 late yesterday; volume still moderate. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support pair at 44.70 level, says local bank trader. Eyes resistance at 44.95. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0227 GMT [Dow Jones] China government bonds higher as liquidity conditions improve with unsuccessful subscription funds for ICBC's (601398.SH) convertible bond issue returning to money market. Shanghai Stock Exchange government bond index at 126.62 vs 126.60 last close, interbank 7-day weighted-average repo rate down 15 bps at 2.35%. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may try to ensure that market liquidity remains ample in coming weeks to meet increasing cash demand ahead of Mid-Autumn Festival late-September," says Beijing-based analyst with local insurer. Tips bond index in 126.6-126.7 range for rest of session. (ming.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0223 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei up 0.4% at 9097.63 midday, with 24 of Topix's 33 subsectors higher. Tech shares higher on Nasdaq's strength, \uc2 Sony\uc2  (6758.TO) up 1.7% at Y2,469, \uc2 Toshiba\uc2  (6502.TO) up 1.3% at Y389. While pension funds may be picking up cheap stocks, both foreign investors and retail investors staying on sidelines before U.S. jobs data out later in global trading day, says Yutaka Miura, senior technical analyst at Mizuho Securities, adding that index may trade between 9000-9150 in afternoon. Matsuya (8237.TO) down 4.8% at Y597 on Nikkei report department store operator Isetan, unit of \uc2 Isetan Mitsukoshi Holdings\uc2  (3099.TO), has decided to end capital and \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  tie-up with Matsuya. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0223 GMT [Dow Jones] DPJ power-broker Ozawa aims to oust PM Kan, but even if Ozawa succeeds, Japan will continue to face major challenges to any effective \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite Ozawa's remark Thursday that government "should definitely" stem strong JPY; that's because Ozawa would be constrained by international expectations \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Osamu Takashima, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy won't change even if a new Ozawa administration takes over, as he will face the same difficulties regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that Kan has." Says chief among them is G20 framework that countries should refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . While framework could change if USD weakness roils markets, says for now it "doesn't have any serious adverse effect on the global economy." Traders say if government were to go ahead with any unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it would likely be too small in scale to have major effect.(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0223 GMT [Dow Jones] HSI nearly flat at 20,872.68, consolidating after 2-day, 1.6% rally; volume spikes to HK$16.49 billion, but boosted by more than HK$1 billion from Ping An (2318.HK) after Newbridge Asia sells down stake. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  remains bullish on HK market, says historically, average length of earnings expansion cycle in MSCI HK about 26 months; "currently, we are only 10 months into this cycle." House's year-end target for HSI at 26,193. Ping An +3.6% at HK$68.45 as Newbridge's stake sale viewed as lifting overhang, is best-performing blue chip; worst performer Esprit (0330.HK), slumps 5.4% to HK$40.60 in further post-results weakness. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0219 GMT [Dow Jones] Bank Negara likely to keep policy rates unchanged for remainder of year after maintaining key rate at 2.75% yesterday, says OSK Research. Following Thursday's policy decision, "we revised our year-end forecast for OPR from 3.00% to 2.75%," house says. OSK expects resumption of rate hikes in latter half of next year, possibly in 3Q. "For 2011, contingent on the global economic recovery and, subsequently, the timing of the Fed rate hike, we forecast the OPR to be raised to 3.50% by end-2011," house says. Adds, given strong growth momentum in 1H, current official forecast of 4.5%-5.5% growth may be revised higher during Budget 2011 announcement in October. OSK expects growth at 7.5% for the year. OSK also says \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  might have 8 meetings in 2011, rather than 6 they have currently set, given uncertainties in global financial markets. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0216 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares likely higher, supported by gains in most regional markets, firm IDR, traders say; tip benchmark index in 3110-3140 range today after ending down 0.4% yesterday at 3122.149. "Overall, I think the market will continue to consolidate ahead of the Bank Indonesia's policy rate meeting later today but bargain-buying by local funds may drive the main index slightly higher," says trader at Lautandhana Securities. Coal miner Bumi (BUMI.JK), palm oil producer Sampoerna Agro (SGRO.JK) may lead gains, thanks to higher commodity prices, but Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) may fall on profit-taking after recent outperformance. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0216 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD lower at 31.987 vs 32.040 at yesterday's close. Dealer from foreign bank says trading thin ahead of U.S. nonfarm payrolls data due later in day, although overall positive market sentiment lends some strength to TWD. Tips tight 31.940-32.040 band today. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again before closing; it has been actively selling TWD in market in recent months, traders believe \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to keep USD/TWD at around 32.000 so as not to hurt competitiveness of exports sector. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0215 GMT [Dow Jones] Silver slightly lower at $19.61, down 4 cents after rising 1.5% overnight, with May high of $19.81 in sight, says ScotiaMocatta. "We are bullish on silver looking for an eventual test of the 2008 high of $21.35." Adds gold/silver ratio broke lower through August low of 64.30 to current 63.72. Tips April low of 62.66 as next major support followed by 2010 low of 60.77. Silver leading gilded life, tracking gold and also getting boost when industrial metals rise, although doesn't seem to suffer when base metals fall as long as gold remains firm. (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0213 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude to take cue from U.S. job data due later today; gains over past two sessions should be viewed as upwards correction after overselling, August unemployment result to set direction a