\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Gains Vs. Euro Ahead Of ECB, Slips Vs. Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Twaronite  \par \uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2010\par 10:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 The euro edged down against the dollar in Asian trading Thursday ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting later in the session.\par \par \uc2 The bank will announce its interest-rate decision at 1:45 p.m. Frankfurt time, or 7:45 a.m. Eastern. President Jean-Claude Trichet will hold his monthly news conference at 8:30 a.m.\par \par \uc2 The ECB is expected to leave its key lending rate at a record low 1%. The market's main focus will be the tone of Trichet's remarks and whether they reveal deepening concerns about slowing U.S. growth.\par \par \uc2 The euro (CUR_EURUSD) slipped to $1.2786 from $1.2799 in late North American trading on Wednesday. The British pound (CUR_GBPUSD) fell to $1.5383 from $1.5453.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar slipped against its Japanese counterpart, even after a Japanese political candidate reiterated his call for direct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the recently strong yen.\par \par \uc2 Ruling-party presidential candidate Ichiro Ozawa said in a televised debate with his party rival, Prime Minister Naoto Kan, that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's appreciation, even though unilateral action was unlikely to change the long-term trend.\par \par \uc2 "I think the recent rapid pace of the yen's rise means that we probably have to act with due determination," Ozawa said, according to Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 Against the yen (CUR_USDYEN) -- which surged to a 15-year high against the greenback last week -- the dollar slipped to \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A584.15, from \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A584.46 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index (DXY), a measure of the U.S. unit against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose to 82.551, from 82.514 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the dollar rose against the yen but declined against the euro and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a measure of U.S. manufacturing activity unexpectedly improved last month. [ 09-02-10 0429ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020100902e6920001s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
