\par\par \b \uc2 Euro zone support to weaken yen not discussed-sources\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jan Strupczewski   \par \uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2010\par 17:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS, Sept 2 (Reuters) - There have been no discussions about the euro zone joining a potential Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen <JPY=><EURJPY=>, euro zone sources said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The yen has been strengthening against the euro and the dollar, edging up towards a 15-year peak against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, prompting market speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem its rise.\par \par \uc2 Japanese ruling party powerbroker Ichiro Ozawa, challenging Prime Minister Naoto Kan in a party leadership vote, said on Thursday that action was needed to stem rapid rises in the yen.\par \par \uc2 Ozawa said that while a solo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not have much impact, Japanese authorities should be prepared to act.\par \par \uc2 "European support has not been discussed," one euro zone source said. "This is a question that would typically arise in the framework of the G7 or the G20 (groups of leading economies), so we still have a few weeks. So far there have been no such discussions," the official said.\par \par \uc2 A second senior euro zone source also indicated that the euro zone was unlikely to go against the market.\par \par \uc2 "Do not pee into the wind, only with it," the source said.\par \par \uc2 Both sources are officials who are not involved in determining European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy but are familiar with euro zone thinking on the issue.\par \par \uc2 From early 2007 to early 2008 the yen was very weak against the euro at around 168 yen because of carry traders taking advantage of very low Japanese interest rates to borrow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest in higher yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 Euro zone officials then said this not only gave Japan an unfair trading advantage but also deepened global trade and savings imbalances, which if unwound rapidly, could cause a major crisis.\par \par \uc2 Top euro zone officials said in mid-2007 that the exchange rate of the yen against the euro should reflect Japan's fundamentals which were improving.\par \par \uc2 G7 finance ministers warned in February 2007 at their meeting in Essen, Germany, against one-way bets against the yen and the message was then often repeated by the Eurogroup of finance minister later in 2007.\par \par \uc2 But Japan is only the euro zone's 9th biggest trading partner after Britain, the United States, China, Switzerland, Russia, Poland, the Czech Republic and Sweden.\par \par \uc2 Euro zone imports from Japan in January-May totalled 20.2 billion euros and exports to Japan in the same period 13.3 billion euros, which means Japan accounted for 3.4 percent of euro zone imports and bought 2.3 percent of euro zone exports.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jan Strupczewski; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 EUROZONE-JAPAN/YEN|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100902e692001g7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
