\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Time To Look At Long USD/JPY Strategies - RBS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2010\par 12:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1048 GMT [Dow Jones] It's time to look at long USD/JPY strategies, says RBS. Although the market is buying JPY and doubting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will work, RBS thinks it could push USD/JPY back toward 85.00-90.00. The bank says it would be difficult in justifying the market taking on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as Japan's fundamentals are poor and the economy will likely suffer more if the JPY rises further. USD/JPY now at 84.17. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1025 GMT [Dow Jones] The fact that Hungary sold fewer 12-month T-bills than planned at an auction Thursday, indicates low domestic liquidity rather than risk aversion by international investors, one bond trader says. AKK sold HUF35 billion of 12-month treasury bills, below the HUF50 billion target volume. "This isn't such a bad figure, the AKK could have paid more attention to demand at current yield levels, then this auction wouldn't look so bad," he adds. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1024 GMT [Dow Jones] Swiss franc strength has been one of the dominant features in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets recently, and the franc is set to extend its gains to test the December 2008 all-time high at 1.5113 against sterling. See Thursday's Charting Europe column by Francis Bray. (francis.bray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1008 GMT [Dow Jones] French government bond auction results are strong as investors showed up after the cancellation of August's auction, says Ioannis Sokos, strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in London. "With German yields close to record lows, the extra yield offered by French paper looks even more appealing, he says. Separately, Newedge Strategy's economist Annalisa Piazza says that "as expected, demand was solid for all four issues as the French paper looked extremely cheap vs. its German counterparts after the past few weeks' widening movement in cross-country spreads." France sold EUR8.88 billion of OAT bonds, just off the upper end of the EUR7.5 billion to EUR9 billion range. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1006 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end +0.1% at 920.54 (still nearly 14-year-high) in breath-taking heavy volume. Gains in early trade stumbled briefly after court orders withdrawal of license of 2 industrial projects, sinking SET Index to day's low of 912.45. But concerns calmed, with benchmark rebounding quickly, after court says 74 of 76 Map Ta Phut Industrial projects can proceed. "It's good news for the market. The projects (that are not allowed to proceed) don't have significant impact," says Globlex Securities' head of strategist Chakkrit Charoenmethachai. Expects banks, construction plays to still march forward; 912-930 range tipped. Among most active, Banpu (BANPU.TH) +1.3% at THB626, \uc2 Krung Thai Bank\uc2  (KTB.TH) +2.1% at THB14.90. Following 2 licenses ordered to be withdrawn, PTT Chemical (PTTCH.TH) down 3.7% at THB103 vs THB99 after court order, \uc2 Siam Cement\uc2  (SCC.TH) down 0.7% at THB303 vs THB293. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1002 GMT [Dow Jones] Spain's bond auction result was "decent, although not stellar" and it compares unfavorably to the previous Spanish auctions, says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  strategist Chiara Cremonesi. The EUR3.31 billion sold of the 3% April 2015 bond is towards the lower end of the EUR3 billion to EUR4 billion range, while the average yield of 2.964% is slightly below secondary market levels. "On the positive side, the weighted average rate was 2.964% versus 3.02% in the market, hinting at 5bps over-biddding," said separately Ioannis Sokos, strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . "Overall not an impressive auction but still job done by Spanish Tesoro," he says. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1001 GMT [Dow Jones] The fall in the French jobless rate in 2Q is good news for the government and the economy, \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  economist Dominique Barbet says, noting that good news for the government is "something scarce these days." The jobless rate in mainland France fell to 9.3% from 9.5% in 2Q, according to data from Insee. Barbet says the data may also help increase household confidence after ongoing decline since February. (william.horobin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1001 GMT [Dow Jones] AUD/NZD runs into profit taking after a strong Fonterra dairy auction result overnight and meeting resistance in the 1.2800-50 region notes \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . The bank says its technical analysis expected the latter and expects the cross to come under further downside pressure Thursday. AUD/NZD now at 1.2705 from Wednesday's 4 month high around 1.2842. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0952 GMT [Dow Jones] The fall in the French jobless rate should be put in context as new jobs lack long-term security, says Natixis economist Adele Renaux. This reflects significant uncertainty on mid-term activity. Job losses should increase in the coming quarters, even if at a slower pace than in 2009, Renaux says. (william.horobin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0949 GMT [Dow Jones] European credit spreads are tighter and there has been strong buying from retail invertors, after the sell off in rates products saw the price of recently-issued bonds drop below par, \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  says. With bonds in demand, the CDS-cash basis fell from +21bp to +16bp. iTraxx Europe is at 108/109 bps, 4 bps tighter from Wednesday's close. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0949 GMT [Dow Jones] Most Thai government bond prices lower in lackluster trade. Only some medium term notes active due to ample liquidity. Eyes on U.S. non-farm payroll tomorrow, says local dealer. "If the U.S. stocks are good tonight and the yields of U.S. Treasurys rise, there may be some selling pressure in the medium term bonds tomorrow," he adds. Expects yields to move in 10 bps range. Bid/offer yields of issue due December 2015 quoted at 2.59%/2.58% vs 2.60%/2.58% late Wednesday, November 2016 quoted at 2.72%/2.68% vs 2.67%/2.65%, June 2019 quoted at 2.75%/2.67% vs 2.72%/2.70%. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0943 GMT [Dow Jones] JPY could appreciate further as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's troubled politics decreases chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in Japan. DPJ power-broker Ozawa's bid to oust PM Kan could destabilize politics even if Kan survives, as that might prompt Ozawa's faction to bolt party. "While political uncertainty tends to be generally negative for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in Japan's case it can have the opposite effect and generate upward pressure as the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls," Yamamoto says. Instability could also lead to early general election. Says that would mean "the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be reduced, which could increase downside risk to USD/JPY."(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com) [ 09-02-10 0648ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100902e69200076\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
