\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: JPY May Gain On Japan's Troubled Politics -BarCap\b0\par\par\uc2 1,522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2010\par 11:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0943 GMT [Dow Jones] JPY could appreciate further as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's troubled politics decreases chances of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , says Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Japan. DPJ power-broker Ozawa's bid to oust PM Kan could destabilize politics even if Kan survives, as that might prompt Ozawa's faction to bolt party. "While political uncertainty tends to be generally negative for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in Japan's case it can have the opposite effect and generate upward pressure as the likelihood of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  falls," Yamamoto says. Instability could also lead to early general election. Says that would mean "the likelihood of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be reduced, which could increase downside risk to USD/JPY."(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0941 GMT [Dow Jones] Investors are increasingly turning to the Swiss franc as a proxy for the old Deutschmark says \uc2 UBS\uc2 . Switzerland's strong economy, massive foreign reserves, traditional safe-haven status and close links with the German economy have drawn investors in the wake of the euro zone debt crisis. \uc2 UBS\uc2  says Thursday's Swiss 2Q GDP data confirm Switzerland is matching Germany's economic performance and is outperforming the euro zone. It says Switzerland's strong fundamentals have already resulted in the franc printing lifetime highs against the euro and it expects the franc to remain strong throughout the remainder of this decade. EUR/CHF now at 1.2964. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0940 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/THB at 31.15 vs 31.16 late yesterday in thin trade. Pair drifts higher to 31.20-31.21 early as market was worried today's early-morning discussion between Thai PM, economic ministers, \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 's governor would yield measures. "The comments are in the direction that it's hard for the baht to go against the tide. Exporters have to adjust themselves," says dealer. Another dealer says players skeptical whether BOT would make any fresh move although BOT's governor said current strong baht not worrisome. Pair tipped 31.13-31.23 range Friday.(piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0935 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD prints the day's high of 1.2837 in the wake of well received French auctions, Spanish 5-yr auction and the euro-zone 2Q GDP revision to +1.9% year on year from +1.7% last. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0933 GMT [Dow Jones]--Wednesday's Czech auction of five-year bonds shows strong demand "once again," Dalimil Vyskovsky, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed-income trade, says. "Less demand from local accounts and primary dealers this time as locals real money seem to have been saturated to a large extent in the recent past, and it probably was the foreign demand behind the 2.5 b/c in the competitive part of the auction," Vyskovsky says. Paper trades at yield 2.435%, down from the Wednesday's average yield at the auction of 2.592%. (leos.rousek@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0931 GMT [Dow Jones] India overnight indexed swaps steady as government bond yields trade in tight 4 bp range, while ample liquidity in banking system keeps away paying interest, says trader with foreign bank. Indian banks parked INR185 billion surplus cash with RBI under daily discount window Thursday. 1-year-OIS rate at 6.16%/6.20% vs 6.16%/6.19% Wednesday close, while 5-year OIS rate at 6.98%/7.02% vs 6.96%/6.99% last close. "The market isn't sure which way the yields are going to move hereafter. Most participants are expecting a rate hike of 25 basis points in key lending and borrowing rates (at Sept. 16 policy review), but the factory output data that will be released prior will be a key indicator of how aggressive the RBI will be," trader says. Tips 1-year OIS rate in 6.05%-6.25% band in week, 5-year OIS rate at 6.90%-7.10% band. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0929 GMT [Dow Jones] Yield spreads on Spanish government bonds over their German counterparts tighten after an auction of 5-year bonds goes through smoothly. Spain sells EUR3.31B of 5-year bonds at an average yield of 2.964%, down from 3.657% at the last auction held in July, and also below secondary market levels prior to the auction. The bid-to-cover ratio is little changed at 1.63 times. 5-year Spanish bond/bobl yield spread is 4 bps tighter at 173.6 bps, while the 10-year yield spread over bunds is 2.6 bps tighter at 168.2 bps. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds slip after euro-zone GDP on-year growth rate is revised up and a Spanish bond auction goes through smoothly. Euro-zone 2Q on-year GDP growth was revised up to show an increase of 1.9% vs initial estimate of 1.7%. The quarter-on-quarter increase was unchanged at 1% from the initial estimate. A Spanish auction of 5-year bonds also went off well, with the average yield coming in below market levels and a decent cover ratio of 1.63. September bunds are down 0.27 at 132.96. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0923 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end down 0.4% at 3122.149 in moderate volume, off intraday high of 3157.763, as many investors prefer to hold cash ahead of Bank Indonesia's rate meeting tomorrow and long holiday next week, traders say; expect shares to continue to consolidate tomorrow; tip index at 3100-3150 range. "Profit-taking by foreign funds weighed down overall sentiment here, shrugging off gains in most Asian markets," says trader at First Asia Capital. Indonesian markets will be closed Sept. 4-14. Among decliners, coal miner Adaro (ADRO.JK) down 4.3% at IDR1,780 on further selling after reporting weak 1H earnings early this week, while coal miner \uc2 Indo Tambangraya\uc2  (ITMG.JK) down 5.6% at IDR37,100 after parent sells 8.72% stake at ITMG at 8% discount to yesterday's close. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0918 GMT [Dow Jones] Pakistan shares trade tad higher, led by refinery and cement plays. Benchmark KSE-100 index +0.2% at 9756.30. "Some buying interest has returned, mainly in cement and oil sector after the recent correction," says a dealer. Cement plays are attracting investments on hopes sales could pick up as the government will have to spend large sums of cash to rebuild infrastructure affected by recent floods, he added. An analyst says, "The future course of the market is dependent upon the outcome of the meeting between the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and International Monetary Fund officials." If the IMF relaxes the conditions, such as the widening of fiscal deficit, the rise in inflation rate, increasing amount of borrowing from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to plug budgetary deficit and deferring electricity tariff, then some sanity is likely to prevail at the local bourse, the analyst says. Economy is likely to slow in FY11 (starting July) from earlier growth estimates of 4.5% and may range from 2% to 2.5% as floods could lead to economic loss of around $4 billion. Bestway Cement (BWCL.KA) +5.4% at PKR19.39, Attock Refinery (ATRL.KA) +2.1% at PKR81.01. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0913 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia shares end higher for fifth consecutive day, benchmark KLCI +0.6% at 1441.07 at fresh 31-month closing high with sentiment buoyed by stronger regional markets. Local dealer says all-round gains led by techs, consumer, property stocks on stronger institutional interest; tips next resistance at 1450. Affin Investment says keeping its Overweight call on KLCI, year-end target at 1490, but concerned that "upside potential for the KLCI between now and end of this year is limited... we think KLCI will likely run into a short-term loss in momentum, if not weaken, but followed by a re-acceleration next year." Market breadth positive with 511 advancers vs 256 decliners; AirAsia (5099.KU) +8.0% at MYR1.89, BAT (4162.KU) +3.2% at MYR46.96, \uc2 Petronas Dagangan\uc2  (5681.KU) +7.4% at MYR11.60, UEM Land (5148.KU) +7.6% at MYR1.84, Top Glove (7113.KU) down 1.8% at MYR6.08. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0908 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR a touch lower at 9,008 in late trade vs 9,010 yesterday, 8,995 intraday low, as players cover short positions built yesterday on milder-than-expected August inflation, dealers say. "Trade is slightly subdued in the late session as players have set one eye for tomorrow," when Bank Indonesia announces its rate decision, dealer says; adds tips 8,980-9,020 range Friday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to keep key interest rate steady at 6.5% tommorow, according to Dow Jones poll. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com) [ 09-02-10 0543ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100902e6920006f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
